{"hits": {"hits": [{"updated": "2024-09-16T18:09:16.057817+00:00", "created": "1999-04-07T00:00:00+00:00", "id": "1115226", "metadata": {"authors": [{"full_name_unicode_normalized": "feynman, richard p.", "full_name": "Feynman, Richard P.", "curated_relation": true, "record": {"$ref": "https://inspirehep.net/api/authors/1010044"}, "affiliations": [{"record": {"$ref": "https://inspirehep.net/api/institutions/902711"}, "value": "Caltech"}], "ids": [{"schema": "INSPIRE ID", "value": "INSPIRE-00000031"}, {"schema": "INSPIRE BAI", "value": "Richard.P.Feynman.1"}], "last_name": "Feynman", "signature_block": "FYNANr", "first_name": "Richard P.", "uuid": "ec78b827-3e6f-420e-9957-c7c5b24a2009", "recid": 1010044}], "citation_count_without_self_citations": 5254, "citation_count": 5254, "publication_info": [{"journal_volume": "21", "page_end": "488", "year": 1982, "journal_record": {"$ref": "https://inspirehep.net/api/journals/1214707"}, "page_start": "467", "journal_title": "Int.J.Theor.Phys."}, {"page_end": "944", "page_start": "923", "parent_record": {"$ref": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/540341"}}], "citeable": true, "$schema": "https://inspirehep.net/schemas/records/hep.json", "number_of_pages": 22, "legacy_version": "20180416092258.0", "inspire_categories": [{"term": "Computing"}], "legacy_creation_date": "1999-04-07", "preprint_date": "1981-05", "author_count": 1, "first_author": {"affiliations_identifiers": [{"schema": "ROR", "value": "https://ror.org/05dxps055"}], "full_name": "Feynman, Richard P.", "ids": [{"schema": "INSPIRE ID", "value": "INSPIRE-00000031"}, {"schema": "INSPIRE BAI", "value": "Richard.P.Feynman.1"}], "last_name": "Feynman", "first_name": "Richard P.", "recid": 1010044}, "control_number": 1115226, "dois": [{"value": "10.1007/BF02650179"}], "earliest_date": "1981-05", "document_type": ["article"], "texkeys": ["Feynman:1981tf"], "abstracts": [{"value": "On the program it says this is a keynote speech--and I don't know what a keynote speech is. I do not intend in any way to suggest what should be in this meeting as a keynote of the subjects or anything like that. I have my own things to say and to talk about and there's no implication that anybody needs to talk about the same thing or anything like it. So what I want to talk about is what Mike Dertouzos suggested that nobody would talk about. I want to talk about the problem of simulating physics with computers and I mean that in a specific way which I am going to explain. The reason for doing this is something that I learned about from Ed Fredkin, and my entire interest in the subject has been inspired by him. It has to do with learning something about the possibilities of computers, and also something about possibilities in physics. If we suppose that we know all the physical laws perfectly, of course we don't have to pay any attention to computers. It's interesting anyway to entertain oneself with the idea that we've got something to learn about physical laws; and if I take a relaxed view here (after all I'm here and not at home) I'll admit that we don't understand everything."}], "refereed": true, "titles": [{"title": "Simulating physics with computers"}, {"source": "arXiv", "title": "Simulating physics with computers."}], "external_system_identifiers": [{"schema": "SPIRES", "value": "SPIRES-9599207"}, {"schema": "MSNET", "value": "658311"}, {"schema": "ADS", "value": "1982IJTP...21..467F"}], "facet_author_name": ["1010044_Richard P. Feynman"], "_oai": {"sets": ["Literature"], "id": "oai:inspirehep.net:1115226", "updated": "2024-09-16T18:09:16.057817"}, "curated": true, "journal_title_variants": ["Int. J. Theor. Phys.", "Int.J.Theor.Phys."]}, "links": {"bibtex": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/1115226?format=bibtex", "latex-eu": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/1115226?format=latex-eu", "latex-us": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/1115226?format=latex-us", "json": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/1115226?format=json", "json-ex